.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWNFILE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clownfile
.Nd clown per-instance configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Nm
is a TOML file that sets per-directory defaults for a clown session (RFC-0013).
clown discovers clownfiles by ascending from the current directory to
.Ev HOME ,
merging them so a
.Nm
closer to the current directory overrides one closer to
.Ev HOME ,
per key.
An absent
.Nm
is not an error; a malformed one is.
.Pp
This page documents the
.Sy [profile]
table (run defaults) and the
.Sy [attach]
table (multiplexer self-wrap templates).
.Ss [profile]
The
.Sy [profile]
table provides defaults layered beneath explicit command-line flags and
environment variables.
The named-profile registry
.Pq Fl -profile
is a separate mechanism and wins over these defaults.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy provider
The provider (claude, codex, circus, opencode, crush).
Applied only when neither
.Fl -provider
nor
.Ev CLOWN_PROVIDER
is set; a clownfile provider also suppresses the interactive profile picker.
.It Sy backend
The tent container backend (podman or lima) used by
.Fl -tent .
.It Sy model
The model.
Injected as
.Fl -model
for the claude-family providers (claude, circus, clownbox) when the user has not
already passed
.Fl -model ;
other providers source their model elsewhere.
.It Sy [profile.env]
A table of environment variables exported into the provider and its plugin
servers, set only when not already present (the ambient environment wins).
.El
.Ss [attach]
The
.Sy [attach]
table is clown's multiplexer/attach layer (RFC-0013 §1.3).
When
.Sy multiplexer
is set to a value other than
.Ql none ,
clown wraps itself in the configured multiplexer on boot \(em "implicit
per-instance attach" \(em by re-exec'ing the resolved template before launching
the provider.
The placeholder
.Ql {id}
expands to the per-instance session key and the exact element
.Ql {entry}
splices clown's own entrypoint argv;
.Ql {prompt}
and
.Ql {dir}
are available to the spawn templates only.
An unrecognized placeholder is rejected.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy multiplexer
.Ql zmx
or
.Ql none .
.Ql none
(and an absent
.Sy [attach] )
runs clown inline.
.It Sy start
The argv template clown re-execs into for a fresh interactive launch.
.It Sy resume
The argv template clown re-execs into for a reattach (a forwarded
.Fl -resume ,
.Fl r ,
or
.Fl -session-id ,
or
.Nm clown resume ) .
.It Sy resume-title
A string emitted as an OSC-2 terminal title before a resume attach
.Pq Ql {id} No is substituted .
.It Sy spawn , Sy spawn-entry , Sy spawn-window
Detached-worker templates.
This release parses and holds them as the single-source schema but does not
execute them; their executor is an open question (RFC-0013 §1.3).
.El
.Pp
clown self-execs
.Sy start
and
.Sy resume
only when an interactive terminal is present;
.Ev CLOWN_ATTACH_FORCE Ns = Ns Ql 1
overrides that check for unusual terminals.
Remote (ssh) attach is out of scope and remains spinclass's.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[profile]
provider = "claude"
model = "claude-sonnet-4-6"

[profile.env]
ANTHROPIC_LOG = "info"

[attach]
multiplexer = "zmx"
start = ["zmx", "attach", "{id}", "{entry}"]
resume = ["zmx", "attach", "{id}", "{entry}"]
resume-title = "{id}"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown-chat 1 ,
.Xr clown-job 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC-0013 (clownfile, per-instance identity, and clown-owned chat).
